  "_skill_md": "---\nname: polymarket\ndescription: Internal API for polymarket\nmetadata:\n  author: unbrowse\n  version: \"1.0\"\n  baseUrl: \"https://gamma-api.polymarket.com\"\n  authMethod: \"Bearer Token\"\n  endpointCount: 13\n  apiType: \"internal\"\n  category: \"web-app\"\n---\n\n# Polymarket API\n\n> Reverse-engineered internal API. Unofficial — may change without notice.\n\n## Documentation Index\n- `SKILL.md` (this file)\n- `references/REFERENCE.md` (detailed endpoint docs)\n- `references/ENDPOINTS.json` (machine-readable endpoint catalog)\n- `scripts/api.ts` (typed client interface)\n\n## Authentication\nBearer Token — Authentication method detected from captured traffic.\n\n### Providing credentials\n- Prefer passing auth as request headers or cookies at call time (do not hardcode secrets into the skill).\n- If executing via an external proxy/executor, pass per-call credentials (cookies and/or headers) so they are not persisted.\n\n## Dependencies\n- Runtime capable of HTTPS requests.\n- If using `scripts/api.ts`: TypeScript toolchain (or transpile to JS).\n\n## Endpoints\n\n### Auth Flow (1)\n- `GET /_next/static/{staticToken}/_clientmiddlewaremanifest.json` — Get client middleware manifest (auth)\n\n### Data Read (1)\n- `GET /{id}` — Read data by ID\n\n### Data Write (2)\n- `POST /{id}` — Write data by ID\n- `POST /v1/{v1Id}` — Write data using v1 ID\n\n### Search (1)\n- `GET /cm/s` — Search for content\n\n### Media (1)\n- `GET /_next/image` — Retrieve an image\n\n### Realtime (2)\n- `GET /events/pagination` — Fetch paginated events\n- `GET /events/slug/{slugId}` — Fetch events by slug ID\n\n### Config (4)\n- `GET /api/magic-client/{magic-clientId}/config` — Get Magic client configuration\n- `GET /config/com/{comId}.json` — Get community configuration\n- `GET /flags/v0/config.json` — Get feature flag configuration\n- `GET /v1/projects/{projectId}/settings` — Get project settings\n\n### Core API (1)\n- `HEAD /` — Check if the API is available\n\n## Quick Start\n\n### OpenClaw (Unbrowse) workflow\n- Authenticate in the browser first (no credentials are shipped with this skill).\n- Capture fresh auth locally: run `unbrowse_capture` on an authenticated page for this domain.\n- Execute via backend gate + client browser executor: `unbrowse_replay` with `executionMode=\"backend\"`.\n\nExample:\n```text\nunbrowse_replay { service: \"polymarket\", executionMode: \"backend\", endpoint: \"GET /{id}\" }\n```\n\nHere are a few quick examples to get you started:\n\n```typescript\n// Fetching data by ID\nasync function fetchData(id: string) {\n  try {\n    const data = await client.get({ id });\n    console.log(\"Data:\", data);\n    return data;\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.error(\"Error fetching data:\", error);\n    return null;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```typescript\n// Writing data by ID\nasync function writeData(id: string, payload: any) {\n  try {\n    const response = await client.post({ id, data: payload });\n    console.log(\"Write Response:\", response);\n    return response;\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.error(\"Error writing data:\", error);\n    return null;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Additional Notes\n\n**Type:** Reverse-engineered internal API (unofficial)\n**Auth:** Bearer Token\n**Base URL:** `https://gamma-api.polymarket.com`\n**Captured Auth:** 3 auth headers, 33 session cookies\n\n## About This Skill\n\nThis skill provides access to Polymarket's internal API — the hidden endpoints that power their web/mobile app.\nThese are NOT official public APIs. They were captured by observing network traffic while using the site.\n\n**Important:**\n- Auth tokens in `auth.json` may expire — re-capture if you get 401 errors\n- Internal APIs can change without notice — endpoints may break\n- Rate limits are unknown — be conservative with request frequency\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill when you need to:\n- Access Polymarket data without official API access\n- Automate actions on gamma-api.polymarket.com (faster than browser automation)\n- Call the same endpoints the Polymarket frontend uses\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```typescript\nimport { PolymarketClient } from \"./scripts/api.ts\";\n\n// Load captured auth from auth.json\nconst client = await PolymarketClient.fromAuthFile(\"auth.json\");\n\n// Make requests to internal endpoints\nconst result = await client.get(\"/endpoint\");\n```\n\n## Captured Authentication\n\nThe `auth.json` file contains credentials extracted from browser traffic:\n- **Auth headers:** 3 (sec-fetch-storage-access, x-magic-api-key, authorization)\n- **Session cookies:** 33\n\nIf auth expires, re-run `unbrowse_login` or `unbrowse_capture` to refresh tokens.\n\n## Internal Endpoints (24)\n\n\n## Error Handling\n\n```typescript\ntry {\n  const data = await client.get(\"/resource\");\n} catch (err) {\n  if (err.message.includes(\"401\")) {\n    // Auth expired — need to re-capture\n    console.error(\"Auth expired, re-run unbrowse_login\");\n  } else {\n    console.error(\"API error:\", err.message);\n  }\n}\n```\n\nSee [REFERENCE.md](references/REFERENCE.md) for detailed endpoint documentation.\n"
